<title>JAPAN: Fuji Bank mulling bond issue -- sources.</title>
<headline>Fuji Bank mulling bond issue -- sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fuji Bank Ltd is considering raising funds on the overseas market by issuing corporate bonds, underwriting sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>If Fuji decided on the issue, it would likely be Euroyen convertible bonds in volume of between 100 billion and 200 billion yen, they said.</p>
<p>Fuji was considering the issue to increase its capital, they said.</p>
<p>A Fuji spokesman said the company had nothing to say about a bond issue.</p>
</text>
